{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1017 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "40ac0cca738b4162da39c6ab8b80e551ea28749eef238c4bb9128f7c45590d54" :edb/db-before-t 1016 :edb/db-after-t 1017 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534329 50 #inst "2026-10-06T16:08:24.643Z" 13194139534329 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283582 13194139534329 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283603 13194139534329 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283607 13194139534329 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283589 13194139534329 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283596 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283583 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1089 "q-104431" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1100 "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A)=4-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1113 #uuid "0a2a2113-9f29-565e-aae5-a6794706421f" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283582 1145 "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=4-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =2-k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283584 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283585 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283586 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283587 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283588 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1041 "selection" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283585 13194139534329 true] [17592186283583 1110 #uuid "a073bd65-687d-5e37-a1da-2b80521776eb" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283584 1034 "2" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283584 1111 #uuid "e0d15c03-982d-5609-ae43-1aa5a02e4e97" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283585 1034 "1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283585 1111 #uuid "5235ddc8-c95c-5d69-8fbb-4e14cf8db03d" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283586 1034 "0" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283586 1111 #uuid "a71f6336-91b3-5e54-a482-8aea120d420d" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283587 1034 "-1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283587 1111 #uuid "5cf21e88-dd9f-5184-a368-9e759f74739e" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283588 1034 "-2" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283588 1111 #uuid "633ed4a5-ead4-563e-839d-486ec384fb6f" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283590 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1089 "q-18282" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $-2.$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1113 #uuid "fd79571b-cfb2-59c8-988f-2f68aa4f8bff" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283589 1145 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3-0) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-3)=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283591 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283592 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283593 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283594 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283595 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1041 "selection" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283594 13194139534329 true] [17592186283590 1110 #uuid "8e6cccca-2231-5967-98d5-a3adff05ceef" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283591 1034 "3" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283591 1111 #uuid "c0bc6aa3-0324-5615-b408-ec5db1ead663" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283592 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283592 1111 #uuid "aae2140c-abab-5841-af79-8cb5f5c92f78" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283593 1034 "-3" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283593 1111 #uuid "6ea24c0c-a596-54af-b532-a3f976fc9ca4" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283594 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283594 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283594 1111 #uuid "b89d9b12-10de-5e84-8c9f-c9465a307bec" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283595 1034 "-1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283595 1111 #uuid "4c5f6c56-c45f-5c45-ae15-a45910236188" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283597 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1089 "q-18285" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1113 #uuid "56f56a99-ae3f-56b5-9e3f-612f5a2d8c37" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283596 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-0+(0-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283598 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283599 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283600 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283601 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283602 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1041 "selection" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283599 13194139534329 true] [17592186283597 1110 #uuid "8233a48f-b290-5757-8915-04df2ffaa58e" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283598 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283598 1111 #uuid "3061cdb9-3f5e-578e-aa48-1b24ed90d2f6" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283599 1034 "1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283599 1111 #uuid "dd879f56-1774-57f5-bdfa-3ece34b0c42c" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283600 1034 "0" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283600 1111 #uuid "3259e6e4-8f4a-5a93-a58a-3f5ccd7b0794" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283601 1034 "-1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283601 1111 #uuid "8cc7dec1-6220-541d-b15c-f7806182ca52" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283602 1034 "-2" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283602 1111 #uuid "092a7670-38a2-597e-8b3c-c65a3e952468" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283604 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1089 "q-319443" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1100 "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1113 #uuid "b0a5c074-ab5e-5f2d-8088-6f6048cd7aa6" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283603 1145 "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(k-2)}\\cdot (k+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+2}{\\,k-2\\,} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(k+2) & =-(k-2) \\\\ 2k+4 & =-k+2 \\\\ 3k & =-2 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283605 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283606 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1041 "field-1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283605 13194139534329 true] [17592186283604 1110 #uuid "b02084d4-6c21-50e9-8635-0903f6bf1a7d" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283605 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283605 1111 #uuid "15721863-0e64-5037-8661-654f92161b15" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283606 1034 "0" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283606 1111 #uuid "4f3874f7-33ac-5785-95fd-5b1821b277e4" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283608 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1089 "q-319937" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1100 "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1113 #uuid "29d3d120-8727-55cb-a11c-325a9dc83c87" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283607 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283609 13194139534329 true] [17592186283608 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534329 true] [17592186283608 1041 "field-1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283608 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283609 13194139534329 true] [17592186283608 1110 #uuid "8775fdf4-6ce6-5e46-bc25-de993144ee74" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283609 1034 "1" 13194139534329 true] [17592186283609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534329 true] [17592186283609 1111 #uuid "e3b81913-a3e1-5578-afe1-bc783b842a92" 13194139534329 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-104431" 17592186283582 "q-104431/selection" 17592186283583 "q-104431/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c4390